. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 *
. 
.         *********************************************************************
> *******
.         *Verbal description of the model:       
.         * Postmaterialistic attitudes (variables: plh0056 and plh0061 
.         * from the Inglehart index, collected in 2006 and 2016) 
.         * are used as a proxy for individual support for gender equality 
.         * because postmaterialist values are strongly and positively 
.         * correlated with support for gender equality: if postmaterialist val
> ues are 
.         * stronger in 2016 than in 2006, this indicates a stronger support fo
> r 
.         * gender equality.
.         
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with the chang
> e score 
.         * of postmaterialist values between 2006 and 2016 (variable: ingledif
> f) 
.         * as dependent variable and the dummy variables daughter and sex (var
> iable: 
.         * male) as independent variables. 
.         * To test whether having daughters leads to a larger increase in the 
> support 
.         * of gender equality for men than for women (hypothesis 4), we includ
> e an 
.         * interaction between the variables daughter and male. 
.         * We further control for age in the model. 
.         * We estimate robust standard errors. 
.         * The regression is weighted (weight: phrf).
.         *********************************************************************
> *******
. 
.         reg inglediff i.daughter##i.male age if filter == 1 [aw=phrf], vce(r)
(sum of wgt is 12,626,429.01)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =      4,069
                                                F(4, 4064)        =       2.69
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0293
                                                R-squared         =     0.0051
                                                Root MSE          =     .59962

